From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_gpu: clean up shared area when open fails

open() creates the shared-info area before completing device
initialization. If a later step fails, the existing error path deletes
the framebuffer area but leaves the shared-info area allocated.

framebufferArea / sharedArea were left at zero when an earlier
open() step failed, so the error path could call delete_area() on
an area that had not been created.

Initialize both area IDs to -1 before they can be used, and
release the shared-info area on open failure.

Follow-up to review on change 11824.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/virtio/virtio_gpu.cpp
@@ -568,6 +568,9 @@ virtio_gpu_open(void* _info, const char* path, int openMode, void** _cookie)
 	if (handle == NULL)
 		return B_NO_MEMORY;
 
+	info->sharedArea = -1;
+	info->framebufferArea = -1;
+
 	info->commandDone = create_sem(1, "virtio_gpu_command");
 	if (info->commandDone < B_OK)
 		goto error;
@@ -642,6 +645,8 @@ virtio_gpu_open(void* _info, const char* path, int openMode, void** _cookie)
 error:
 	delete_area(info->framebufferArea);
 	info->framebufferArea = -1;
+	delete_area(info->sharedArea);
+	info->sharedArea = -1;
 	delete_sem(info->commandDone);
 	info->commandDone = -1;
 	free(handle);
@@ -810,8 +815,11 @@ virtio_gpu_init_driver(device_node* node, void** cookie)
 		return B_NO_MEMORY;
 
 	memset(info, 0, sizeof(*info));
+
+	info->framebufferArea = -1;
+	info->sharedArea = -1;
 
 	info->node = node;
 
 	*cookie = info;
 	return B_OK;
-- 
